"""Retrieval helpers: a small document store, PDF text extraction and text chunking.

Why a wrapper: the rest of the code depends on `DocumentStore.add()` and `.search()`, not on
{% if ai_kind == "lancedb" %}LanceDB{% else %}ChromaDB{% endif %}'s own API, so changing the vector store (for example ChromaDB -> LanceDB to move to
Python 3.15) touches this one file.

{%- if ai_kind == "lancedb" %}
Embeddings run locally with model2vec's potion-retrieval-32M: static embeddings, so no PyTorch and
very fast on CPU, at somewhat lower retrieval quality than transformer models. English-focused.
The model is downloaded once at a pinned revision and cached; container images bake it in.
{%- else %}
Embeddings run locally with Chroma's built-in all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (ONNX): 384 dimensions,
English-focused, and input longer than 256 tokens is cut off. The model (about 80 MB) is
downloaded on first use and cached; container images bake it in.
{%- endif %}
Split long documents with `chunk_text()` before adding them: smaller chunks retrieve better.
"""

